    "question": "A monkey swings from branch to branch at an average distance of 1.2 meters per second. How far will a monkey swing in meters if it consistently swings from branches for 30 minutes?",
    "gold": "2160",
    "answer": "If a monkey swings 1.2 meters a second then a monkey can swing 1.2 meters/second * 60 seconds/minute = <<1.2*60=72>>72 meters in a minute.\nIf a monkey swings 72 meters in a minute then a monkey can swing 72 meters/min * 30 minutes = <<72*30=2160>>2,160 meters in 30 minutes\n#### 2160"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how far a monkey will swing in 30 minutes, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert the time from minutes to seconds:**\n   \\[\n   30 \\text{ minutes} = 30 \\times 60 \\text{ seconds} = 1800 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Determine the distance the monkey swings per second:**\n   The monkey swings at an average distance of 1.2 meters per second.\n\n3. **Calculate the total distance swung in 1800 seconds:**\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = \\text{Distance per second} \\times \\text{Total time in seconds}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   \\text{Total distance} = 1.2 \\text{ meters/second} \\times 1800 \\text{ seconds}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Perform the multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   1.2 \\times 1800 = 2160\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the total distance the monkey will swing in 30 minutes is \\(\\boxed{2160}\\) meters.",
